  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dairy sector training programme, Kosovo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In September, 2017, the Netherlands embassy in Pristina, Kosovo and the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO) initiated a project to further develop the Kosovo dairy sector by implementing a training project for the Kosovo Association of Milk Producers (KAMP) extension workers and dairy farmers. This present project can be classified as a follow-up on the initial project. The current project will continue training in feeding management, forage crop production and some new technical areas. The project aims to increase the productivity of dairy farmers and enhance milk quality and production in Kosovo. Furthermore, the project will strengthen the KAMP&apos;s effectiveness by training KAMP&apos;s extension workers and organizational coaching.</narrative>
  </description>
